First Author: Linse
Title: A machine learning model for prediction of 30-day primary graft failure after heart transplantation
Source number: 29  ￼

Very short summary: This study developed and internally validated an artificial neural network model to predict 30-day primary graft failure (PGF) after heart transplantation using the ISHLT Heart Transplant Registry. Five key findings were: (1) the final cohort included 64,964 adult recipients transplanted between 1994 and 2013; (2) PGF incidence within 30 days was 3.7%; (3) the ANN selected 33 of 77 risk variables as relevant for PGF prediction; (4) the internally validated test-cohort C-index/AUROC was 0.70 (95% CI 0.68–0.71); and (5) the most influential predictors included donor age, recipient diagnosis, mechanical ventilation, female-donor-to-male-recipient sex match, and ischemic time, while the ANN outperformed both the original and recalibrated RADIAL score. Tables 1–4 and Figures 1–2 were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

